abstract: >-
  Data and code release for ClerkBench, a benchmark that measures how long a
  chain of simple, fully specified clerical computation a language model can
  execute byte-perfectly. Includes the byte-exact scorer, every scored task
  instance, every raw model attempt behind the fourteen-configuration board,
  the aggregate data behind every published number, and a one-command rebuild
  that re-scores every attempt and reproduces the board.
